<article class="env-lemma" id="07Z5">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/07Z5">Lemma <span data-tag="07Z5">10.40.7</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a ring, let $M$ be an $R$-module, and let $m \in M$. Then $\mathfrak p \in V(\text{Ann}(m))$ if and only if $m$ does not map to zero in $M_\mathfrak p$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      We may replace $M$ by $Rm \subset M$. Then (1) $\text{Ann}(m) = \text{Ann}(M)$ and (2) $m$ does not map to zero in $M_\mathfrak p$ if and only if $\mathfrak p \in \text{Supp}(M)$. The result now follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/00L2" data-tag="00L2">10.40.5</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>